# workspace-probes.manifest — EVERY PROBE OF scripts/lib/workspaces.py, LISTED.
#
# Read by engine/scripts/workspace-probes.py FROM GIT (HEAD:docs/verification/
# workspace-probes.manifest), never from the working tree. One path per line,
# relative to the repository root; `#` starts a comment.
#
# WHY A LIST, WHEN DISCOVERY USED TO BE STRUCTURAL (2026-09-12, round 6 §7).
# The runner discovered a probe by reading its text: a file that named the
# library and drove an entry point was a probe. Both reviewers showed the
# text rule could be stepped around from inside the work under test — a probe
# reaching the library through `getattr("register" + "_spawn")` spells no entry
# point and was invisible, and UNDISCOVERED IS WORSE THAN RED (route 3 of the
# certification-{sage,frank}-gate-integrity-2026-09-12 audits). A probe is now
# asked because its author LISTED it here and committed the line; the text
# scan is kept as a backstop in the other direction, so a committed file that
# looks like a probe and is not listed is reported UNLISTED and blocks.
#
# A path listed here that does not exist at HEAD is MISSING and blocks; a probe
# leaves by its author's retirement (workspace-probe-retirements.tsv), never by
# deletion and never by dropping its line here.
